  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Support of IOM Activities in Afghanistan Outlined in the 2023 Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan is facing an unprecedented humanitarian crisis with a very real risk of systemic collapse and human catastrophe. In addition to unimaginable human costs, this humanitarian crisis is reversing many of the gains of the last 20 years, including around women&#x2019;s rights. 
 
The objective of this 12-month project is to ensure the continuity of a comprehensive and data-driven response for vulnerable migrants in Afghanistan by addressing the humanitarian post-arrival, protection and health needs of undocumented returnees at the borders and identifying the longer-term needs of returnees and internally displaced persons (IDPs) in key targeted provinces and integrate protection principles throughout the response.</narrative>
  </description>
